[% META
        title = "Accounting Maria → PG Mapping & New-User Setup"
   description = "Maps live MariaDB Ency accounting tables onto the per-SiteName PostgreSQL LedgerSMB Result files, and walks the first test (Shanta) through creating an accounting account."
   roles = "admin,developer"
   TemplateType = "Documentation"
   category = "accounting"
   page_version = "0.1"
   last_updated = "Tue Aug 25 2026"
   site_specific = "false"
   project_id = "233"
   project_code = "ACCON"
%]
[% PageVersion = 'Documentation/AccountingMariaPgMapping.tt,v 0.1 2026/08/25 hermes-agent Exp shanta - Maria-to-PG map + Shanta first-run setup' %]
[% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %]
    [% PageVersion %]
[% END %]

<div class="container">
    [% INCLUDE 'admin/documentation/_doc_header.tt'
        page_title   = 'Accounting Maria → PG Mapping & New-User Setup'
        site_name    = site_name
        user_role    = user_role
        last_updated = last_updated
        page_name    = page_name
        doc_project_id   = project_id
        doc_project_code = project_code %]

    <p class="last-updated">Last Updated | Version 0.1 | Status: DRAFT — mapping from live Result files, not yet applied to a PG database</p>

    <div class="doc-info">
        <p class="doc-body"><strong>Authority:</strong> PostgreSQL table shape comes from
        <code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Accounting/Result/*.pm</code>. Tables are created only by
        in-app schema-compare. There is no second schema file to maintain.
        MariaDB <code>ency</code> is the live development store until clone.</p>
    </div>

    <div id="toc" class="row doc-toc">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 class="doc-h2">Quick Navigation</h2>
            <p class="doc-muted">Jump to section:</p>
            <div class="doc-navrow">
                <a href="#overview" class="doc-navlink">Overview</a>
                <a href="#two-namespaces" class="doc-navlink">Two namespaces</a>
                <a href="#mapping" class="doc-navlink">Table mapping</a>
                <a href="#stay-maria" class="doc-navlink">Stay on Maria</a>
                <a href="#entities" class="doc-navlink">Legal entities</a>
                <a href="#shanta-setup" class="doc-navlink">Shanta first run</a>
                <a href="#project-tracking" class="doc-navlink">Project Tracking</a>
                <a href="#decisions" class="doc-navlink">Decisions</a>
                <a href="#see-also" class="doc-navlink">See Also</a>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="overview" class="doc-h2">1. Overview</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Development of accounting and inventory happens in one MariaDB
            database (<code>ency</code>), rows tagged by SiteName. That is fine for building and
            not fine for production-legal isolation. When a SiteName is ready, a per-site
            PostgreSQL accounting database is created from the PG Result files (schema-compare),
            then the statutory books are cloned into it. The rest of the application stays Maria.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">This document is two things: (1) the table map so clone is defined,
            (2) the first-user walkthrough using SiteName <strong>Shanta</strong> as the test
            creation.</p>
            <p class="doc-warning"><strong>Current fact (verified 2026-08-25):</strong> all 25 PG
            Result files exist and are structurally complete. No PostgreSQL accounting database
            has been created yet. The wizard at
            <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/Accounting/setup') %]">/Accounting/setup</a>
            seeds PG <code>chart</code> and will not run until schema-compare has built that DB.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="two-namespaces" class="doc-h2">2. Two namespaces — do not mix them</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th class="doc-th">Namespace</th>
                        <th class="doc-th">Engine</th>
                        <th class="doc-th">Count</th>
                        <th class="doc-th">Who uses it today</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="doc-td"><code>Ency::Result::Accounting::*</code></td>
                        <td class="doc-td">MariaDB ency</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">41 Result files</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">All live pages: COA, GL, inventory, points, hosting, marketplace</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                        <td class="doc-td"><code>Schema::Accounting::Result::*</code></td>
                        <td class="doc-td">PostgreSQL per SiteName</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">25 Result files</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Almost unused. Chart is the target of the setup wizard.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">App code writes <code>resultset('Accounting::CoaAccount')</code>
            against <strong>DBEncy</strong> (Maria). The PG schema is a separate connect via
            <code>AccountingDB::schema_for_site</code>. Mixing the two in one request is the
            split-brain we must not paper over.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="mapping" class="doc-h2">3. Table mapping (Maria → PG)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Clone means copy <em>rows that belong to that SiteName</em> from
            the Maria table into the matching PG table, transforming columns. PG has no
            <code>sitename</code> column — isolation is the database itself.</p>

            <h3 id="map-books" class="doc-h3">3.1 Statutory books (must land in PG)</h3>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th class="doc-th">Maria Result / table</th>
                        <th class="doc-th">PG Result / table</th>
                        <th class="doc-th">Column notes</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="doc-td">CoaAccount / coa_accounts</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Chart / chart</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">accno, description, category map 1:1. Maria is_contra → PG contra; is_tax → tax; heading_id → heading. PG adds charttype, link, gifi_accno, recon. Filter rows where sitename is the site or NULL (shared seed).</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                        <td class="doc-td">CoaAccountHeading / coa_account_headings</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Chart / chart (charttype = H)</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Headings are rows in the same PG chart table, not a second table.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="doc-td">GlEntry / gl_entries</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Gl / gl</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">reference, description, approved map. Maria post_date → PG transdate. Maria entry_type / sitename / currency have no PG column — keep entry_type in notes or extend the Result (schema-compare) before clone.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                        <td class="doc-td">GlEntryLine / gl_entry_lines</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">AccTrans / acc_trans</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">account_id → chart_id (remap after Chart insert). amount stays signed. trans_id → gl.id.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="doc-td">InventoryCustomerInvoice + Line</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Ar + Invoice</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Customer AR. Need a Customer row first (see 3.3).</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                        <td class="doc-td">InventorySupplierInvoice + Line</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Ap + Invoice</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Vendor AP. Need a Vendor row from InventorySupplier.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="doc-td">InventoryCustomerOrder + Line</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Oe + Orderitems</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Open orders. Cart still writes invoices more than orders today.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                        <td class="doc-td">InventorySupplier</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Vendor / vendor</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Supplier master.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="doc-td">PaymentTransaction</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Payment / payment</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Cash/processor payments attached to AR/AP.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                        <td class="doc-td">CurrencyRate</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Exchangerate / exchangerate</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">FX. Optional for CAD-only Shanta books.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>GATE 1:</strong> Chart + Gl + AccTrans mapping coded and
            round-tripped on a test PG before any other table is cloned.</p>

            <h3 id="map-inv" class="doc-h3">3.2 Inventory (clone later — maybe)</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">User standing rule: inventory <em>may</em> follow accounting to PG.
            Until that decision, these stay Maria even after books clone.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th class="doc-th">Maria Result</th>
                        <th class="doc-th">PG counterpart if cloned</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td class="doc-td">InventoryItem</td><td class="doc-td">Parts / parts</td></tr>
                    <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td">InventoryLocation</td><td class="doc-td">Warehouse / warehouse</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="doc-td">InventoryStockLevel + InventoryTransaction</td><td class="doc-td">Inventory / inventory</td></tr>
                    <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td">InventoryItemBOM</td><td class="doc-td">No PG table yet. Stays Maria. Dynamic BOM still unsolved.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="doc-td">InventoryItemSupplier</td><td class="doc-td">Makemodel / parts+vendor link</td></tr>
                    <tr class="doc-tr-alt"><td class="doc-td">InventoryEquipment, Pallet, Assignment, Consignment*</td><td class="doc-td">No PG equivalent. Stay Maria.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>GATE 2:</strong> explicit go from owner before any inventory
            table is created on PG.</p>

            <h3 id="map-gap" class="doc-h3">3.3 Gaps (no Maria source or no PG target)</h3>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>PG Customer</strong> — no Ency Accounting customer master. AR clone must
                    create Customer rows from invoice bill-to / users. Do not invent a second CRM.</li>
                <li><strong>PG Employee, Department, Project, Tax, Taxmodule, Pricegroup, Partsgroup, Shipto, Defaults</strong>
                    — seed empty or from site config at provision. Not cloned from Maria accounting.</li>
                <li><strong>Maria sitename column</strong> — dropped on clone. One PG DB = one SiteName.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="stay-maria" class="doc-h2">4. Stay on Maria (not statutory books)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">These 41-minus-books tables are application features. They are not
            cloned. One Maria schema for the general app is the maintenance bound.</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>Points: PointAccount, PointLedger, PointPackage, PointRule, SitePointAccount</li>
                <li>Marketplace: MarketplaceListing, MarketplaceCategory</li>
                <li>Hosting / internal currency: HostingAccount, HostingCostConfig, InternalCurrencyAccount, InternalCurrencyTransaction, CryptoTransaction</li>
                <li>Owner extras: BenefactorContribution, FounderRoyaltyConfig, SiteCurrencyPreference, ConfigurationInventory</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="entities" class="doc-h2">5. Legal entities (who gets a PG DB)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">One sole proprietorship owned by Shanta. CSC is the application
            owner. 3d (printing) and BMaster (beekeeping) are operating businesses with inventory.
            Each of CSC, 3d, and BMaster gets its own accounting PG database and reports up to
            Shanta for the T2125 filing. Canonical ham-radio SiteName is <strong>Ve7tit</strong>
            (lowercase v).</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th class="doc-th">SiteName</th>
                        <th class="doc-th">Archetype</th>
                        <th class="doc-th">Accounting module today</th>
                        <th class="doc-th">First test?</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="doc-td">Shanta</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">sole_proprietor</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Not enabled (no site_modules rows)</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">YES — first creation</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                        <td class="doc-td">CSC</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">service_consulting</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">ecommerce enabled</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Later</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="doc-td">3d</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">maker_light_manufacturing</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">ecommerce enabled</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Later (has inventory)</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                        <td class="doc-td">BMaster</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">agriculture_apiary</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Not enabled</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Later (has inventory; farm GIFI 9470)</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="doc-td">Ve7tit</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">sole_proprietor</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Not enabled</td>
                        <td class="doc-td">Hobby books if needed</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="shanta-setup" class="doc-h2">6. Step-by-step: first accounting account (Shanta)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Use this as the new-user script. Shanta is the first test so we
            learn the path before CSC/3d/BMaster. GIFI is left empty on the sole-proprietor
            chart (T2125, not T2).</p>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">Before any click — operators (one-time)</h3>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>PG Result files are already the schema.</strong> Do not write DDL.
                    Path: <code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Accounting/Result/</code> (25 files).</li>
                <li><strong>Create the empty PG template database</strong> using schema-compare
                    against those Result files (not a hand SQL dump). Route (verified
                    Admin.pm):
                    <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/admin/schema_compare') %]">/admin/schema_compare</a>.
                    Target a test PostgreSQL, database name <code>accounting_template</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Prove Chart exists</strong> on that template (empty table, columns
                    match Chart.pm: accno, description, charttype, category, link, gifi_accno, contra).</li>
                <li><strong>GATE 3:</strong> until step 2–3 succeed, skip to step A–C only
                    (Maria-side enable). Do not provision a site DB that cannot be cloned from
                    a proven template.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">A. SiteName and login</h3>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li>Log in as a user who administers SiteName <strong>Shanta</strong>
                    (CSC admin may act for all sites; a site owner only for their own).</li>
                <li>Session SiteName must be Shanta (not CSC). Wrong site = wrong books.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">B. Subscribe the site to Accounting</h3>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li>Open
                    <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/admin/site_modules') %]">/admin/site_modules</a>.</li>
                <li>For SiteName Shanta, enable module <code>accounting</code>
                    (Commerce / E-Commerce also counts). Live check is the site_modules table,
                    not site_map.json.</li>
                <li>Without this, /Accounting/setup redirects: site is not subscribed.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">C. Open the setup wizard</h3>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li>Go to
                    <a class="doc-link" href="[% c.uri_for('/Accounting/setup') %]">/Accounting/setup</a>.</li>
                <li>Expected archetype pre-select: <strong>sole_proprietor</strong>
                    (from <code>root/config/coa_templates/site_map.json</code> key Shanta).</li>
                <li>Do not enable ecommerce overlay for Shanta. Teaching overlay: off.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">D. Provision the site PG database (after GATE 3)</h3>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li>Wizard / owner provision creates <code>shanta_accounting</code> from
                    template <code>accounting_template</code> (AccountingDB::provision_site).
                    Identifiers are server-derived. Never type host/db names in a form.</li>
                <li>Confirm registry row SiteAccountingDb for sitename=Shanta, status=active.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">E. Seed the chart</h3>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li>On the wizard, Review &amp; Seed Chart (base = sole_proprietor, overlays none).</li>
                <li>This writes PG <code>chart</code> via CoaTemplate. It does <em>not</em>
                    write Maria <code>coa_accounts</code>. The existing COA page still reads Maria
                    until cutover. That is expected in this phase.</li>
                <li>Spot-check: cash 1000, AR 1100, AP 2000, GST/HST payable 2100, equity 3000,
                    drawings 3100, professional fees 4200. gifi_accno null on every row.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">F. What Shanta does <em>not</em> do on first run</h3>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>No Maria → PG row clone yet (no live Shanta books to move).</li>
                <li>No AI-generated chart (Ph.2 / todo 2278 — not built).</li>
                <li>No inventory on PG.</li>
                <li>Do not use VE7TIT as the key; the ham site is Ve7tit if you ever add it.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-success"><strong>Done when:</strong> Shanta has accounting module on,
            a reachable <code>shanta_accounting</code> PG DB whose chart table holds the
            sole-proprietor seed, and schema-compare was the only DDL path.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
